ok - a worker stopped by fm-control.sh exit reads as reapable for the prune only when the busy record is gone, the exit marker is present and its last event is done
ok - a worker with no busy record whose pane reads busy is not reapable by the prune, even with state/<id>.control-exit left from an earlier stop
ok - a worker whose busy record is gone and whose old state/<id>.control-exit is still present is not closed while its agent is alive in the pane: the prune backs off and the copy stays
ok - end to end: a verified merge arms the prune, the detached run reaps the copy through the real teardown, and the log says reaped
ok - end to end: a worker stopped with the exit verb before its PR merged, whose pane holds only its treehouse get and idle shell, is pruned through the real teardown with no human step
ok - end to end: a squash-merged copy with ignored files that teardown refuses is removed by the fallback, preserved records first, and teardown then closes the task
ok - end to end: a changed file, an unpushed commit and an unpushed NESTED commit each keep the copy, force nothing, and raise exactly one wake
ok - end to end: a co-tenant's lifecycle lock makes the real teardown refuse, the prune retries later without a wake, and then reaps
